#: ../../../guides/tox_replacement_guide.rst:2
msgid "Replacing tox with uv and Poe the Poet"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/tox_replacement_guide.rst:4
msgid ""
"This guide demonstrates how Poe the Poet and |uv_link| can replace |"
"tox_link| for running tests across multiple python versions and environments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/tox_replacement_guide.rst:190
msgid "<a href=\"https://docs.astral.sh/uv/\" target=\"_blank\">uv</a>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/tox_replacement_guide.rst:194
msgid "<a href=\"https://tox.wiki/\" target=\"_blank\">tox</a>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/tox_replacement_guide.rst:8
msgid "Why replace tox?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/tox_replacement_guide.rst:10
msgid ""
"While tox is a powerful tool for test automation, using Poe the Poet with uv "
"offers comparable expressiveness for many use cases, and several compelling "
"advantages:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/tox_replacement_guide.rst:12
msgid ""
"**Faster execution**: uv is significantly faster than traditional virtualenv "
"tools"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/tox_replacement_guide.rst:13
msgid "**Unified configuration**: everything in ``pyproject.toml``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/tox_replacement_guide.rst:14
msgid "**Better integration**: works seamlessly with your existing uv workflow"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/tox_replacement_guide.rst:15
msgid ""
"**More flexible**: leverage all of Poe the Poet's task composition features"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/tox_replacement_guide.rst:16
msgid "**Simpler syntax**: more intuitive task oriented configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/tox_replacement_guide.rst:20
msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/tox_replacement_guide.rst:22
msgid "Install both uv and Poe the Poet:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/tox_replacement_guide.rst:24
msgid ""
"# Install uv\n"
"curl -LsSf https://astral.sh/uv/install.sh | sh\n"
"\n"
"# Install Poe the Poet\n"
"uv tool install poethepoet"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/tox_replacement_guide.rst:32
msgid ""
"See other installation methods in the `uv installation guide <https://docs."
"astral.sh/uv/getting-started/installation/>`_ and :ref:`Poe the Poet "
"installation guide<Installation>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/tox_replacement_guide.rst:36
msgid "Basic migration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/tox_replacement_guide.rst:38
msgid "A typical ``tox.ini`` file might look like this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/tox_replacement_guide.rst:40
msgid ""
"[tox]\n"
"envlist = py310,py311,py312,py313\n"
"\n"
"[testenv]\n"
"deps = pytest\n"
"       pytest-cov\n"
"commands = pytest tests --cov=mypackage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/tox_replacement_guide.rst:50
msgid ""
"Here's the equivalent configuration using Poe the Poet with the :ref:`uv "
"executor <Uv Executor>`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/tox_replacement_guide.rst:52
msgid ""
"[tool.poe.executor]\n"
"type = \"uv\" # Use the uv executor for all tasks by default\n"
"\n"
"[tool.poe.tasks.test-py39]\n"
"cmd = \"pytest tests --cov=mypackage\"\n"
"executor = {isolated = true, python = \"3.9\"} # Specify python version, and "
"that we want an isolated env\n"
"\n"
"[tool.poe.tasks.test-py310]\n"
"cmd = \"pytest tests --cov=mypackage\"\n"
"executor = {isolated = true, python = \"3.10\"}\n"
"\n"
"[tool.poe.tasks.test-py311]\n"
"cmd = \"pytest tests --cov=mypackage\"\n"
"executor = {isolated = true, python = \"3.11\"}\n"
"\n"
"[tool.poe.tasks.test-py312]\n"
"cmd = \"pytest tests --cov=mypackage\"\n"
"executor = {isolated = true, python = \"3.12\"}\n"
"\n"
"[tool.poe.tasks.test-all]\n"
"sequence = [\"test-py39\", \"test-py310\", \"test-py311\", \"test-py312\"]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/tox_replacement_guide.rst:76
msgid "Run all tests with:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/tox_replacement_guide.rst:78
msgid "poe test-all"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/tox_replacement_guide.rst:82
msgid "Or run tests for a specific version:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/tox_replacement_guide.rst:84
msgid "poe test-py311"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/tox_replacement_guide.rst:90
msgid ""
"See the :ref:`uv executor documentation <Uv Executor>` for a full "
"explanation of these and other available executor options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/tox_replacement_guide.rst:94
msgid "Advanced configurations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/tox_replacement_guide.rst:97
msgid "Testing with different dependency sets"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/tox_replacement_guide.rst:99
msgid ""
"If you need to test against different versions of dependencies (like tox's "
"factors):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/tox_replacement_guide.rst:101
msgid ""
"[tool.poe.tasks.test-django32]\n"
"cmd = \"pytest tests\"\n"
"executor = { isolated = true, python = \"3.11\", group = \"dev\", with = "
"\"django==3.2.*\" }\n"
"\n"
"[tool.poe.tasks.test-django42]\n"
"cmd = \"pytest tests\"\n"
"executor = { isolated = true, python = \"3.11\", group = \"dev\", with = "
"\"django==4.2.*\" }"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/tox_replacement_guide.rst:112
msgid "Testing with optional dependencies"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/tox_replacement_guide.rst:114
msgid ""
"Pick and choose optional or dev dependency groups defined in your "
"``pyproject.toml``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/tox_replacement_guide.rst:116
msgid ""
"[tool.poe.tasks.test-with-extras]\n"
"cmd = \"pytest tests\"\n"
"executor = { extra = \"all\", group = [\"ci\", \"debug\"], no-group = "
"\"docs\" }"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/tox_replacement_guide.rst:123
msgid "Compose testing with other tasks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/tox_replacement_guide.rst:125
msgid "Use sequence tasks to run commands before and after tests:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/tox_replacement_guide.rst:127
msgid ""
"[tool.poe.tasks.lint]\n"
"cmd = \"ruff check .\"\n"
"\n"
"[tool.poe.tasks.test-py311]\n"
"cmd = \"pytest tests --cov=mypackage\"\n"
"executor = { isolated = true, python = \"3.11\" }\n"
"\n"
"[tool.poe.tasks.coverage-report]\n"
"cmd = \"coverage report\"\n"
"\n"
"[tool.poe.tasks.ci]\n"
"sequence = [\"lint\", \"test-py311\", \"coverage-report\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/tox_replacement_guide.rst:142
msgid "Or define a DAG of tasks with task ``deps``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/tox_replacement_guide.rst:144
msgid ""
"[tool.poe.tasks.lint]\n"
"cmd = \"ruff check .\"\n"
"\n"
"[tool.poe.tasks.test-py311]\n"
"cmd = \"pytest tests --cov=mypackage\"\n"
"executor = { isolated = true, python = \"3.11\" }\n"
"deps = [\"lint\"]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/tox_replacement_guide.rst:154
msgid ""
"See the :doc:`guide on task composition<../guides/composition_guide>` for "
"more examples."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/tox_replacement_guide.rst:157
msgid "Parallel execution"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/tox_replacement_guide.rst:159
msgid ""
"tox supports running tests in parallel using the ``-p`` option. Poe the Poet "
"lets you define a parallel task that runs all your test variants "
"concurrently:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/tox_replacement_guide.rst:161
msgid ""
"[tool.poe.tasks.test-parallel]\n"
"parallel = [\"test-py39\", \"test-py310\", \"test-py311\", \"test-py312\"]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/tox_replacement_guide.rst:167
msgid "Environment variables"
msgstr "環境變數"

#: ../../../guides/tox_replacement_guide.rst:169
msgid ""
"tox allows setting environment variables for test runs using the ``setenv`` "
"option. You can achieve the same with Poe the Poet using the ``env`` or "
"``envfile`` options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/tox_replacement_guide.rst:171
msgid "Set environment variables directly:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/tox_replacement_guide.rst:173
msgid ""
"[tool.poe.tasks.test-integration]\n"
"cmd = \"pytest tests/integration\"\n"
"executor = { isolated = true, python = \"3.11\" }\n"
"env = { DATABASE_URL = \"postgresql://localhost/test_db\" }"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/tox_replacement_guide.rst:180
msgid "Or load an envfile for the task:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/tox_replacement_guide.rst:182
msgid ""
"[tool.poe.tasks.test-integration]\n"
"cmd = \"pytest tests/integration\"\n"
"executor = { isolated = true, python = \"3.11\" }\n"
"envfile = \".env.test\""
msgstr ""
